# What `COPY . .` in the Dockerfile may take into the build stage. The build
# reads go.mod, go.sum and the Go source under cmd/ and internal/ and nothing
# else (no package embeds a file), so everything here is dead weight in the
# image build — and .git is worse than that: a CI checkout can leave its
# access token in .git/config, COPY puts that in a build-stage layer, and
# ship.yaml exports every stage's layers to the registry as build cache
# (cache-to mode=max). These patterns match at the context root only.
.git
.claude
bin
dist
docs
.env
*.md
